 location="Midline, above the septum pellucidum and fornix and below the cingulate gyrus, from the rostrum beneath the genu in front to the splenium above the pineal region behind; its fibers spread as the radiations into the centrum semiovale and form the forceps minor and major at either end.",
 subdivisions=[("Rostrum and genu", "prefrontal and orbitofrontal connections (forceps minor)"), ("Body", "premotor, motor, somatosensory and parietal connections"), ("Isthmus", "pre- and postcentral and auditory connections"), ("Splenium", "posterior parietal, temporal and occipital connections (forceps major)")],
 function="Interhemispheric transfer of sensory, motor and cognitive information; coordination of bimanual movements; transfer of visual information from the right hemisphere to left-hemisphere language areas.",
