 imaging=img([view("sagittal", 0, 0, 20, "rostrum, genu, body and splenium on the midline"), view("coronal", 0, 0, 20, "body of the callosum forming the roof of the lateral ventricles")],
     "The bright white arch on midline sagittal T1; thinning of the body or splenium suggests chronic white matter disease or hydrocephalus, and callosal lesions perpendicular to the ventricles (Dawson's fingers) on sagittal FLAIR are characteristic of multiple sclerosis.",
     [pathol("Multiple sclerosis", "MRI", "Ovoid FLAIR-bright lesions at the callososeptal interface and perpendicular to the callosum on sagittal FLAIR.", sequence="FLAIR"), pathol("Diffuse axonal injury", "MRI", "Microhemorrhages in the splenium and body on SWI after rotational trauma; associated with poor outcome.", sequence="SWI"), pathol("Butterfly glioblastoma or lymphoma", "MRI", "Enhancing mass crossing the callosum into both hemispheres; lymphoma is homogeneously enhancing and restricts diffusion.", sequence="T1+Gd"), pathol("Cytotoxic lesion of the splenium", "MRI", "Transient oval restriction in the splenium with encephalitis, antiepileptic withdrawal or metabolic disturbance; reversible.", sequence="DWI"), pathol("Agenesis of the corpus callosum", "MRI", "Absent callosum with parallel lateral ventricles (racing car sign), colpocephaly and radially oriented medial gyri.", sequence="T1")],
     "Sagittal FLAIR and T1; SWI for trauma; DWI"),
